<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Examples</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An example illustrating a mistake made by the GPT-4o model on the Correctness attribute: In this case, both the chosen and rejected rationales provide incorrect final answers. However, GPT-4o assigns a correctness score of 1.0 to the chosen rationale, failing to recognize the error in the solution.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F78" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11026v1/Images/GPT4o_mistake.png" id="A1.F78.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:521/274;" width="521" height="274" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 78: </span>An example of a scoring error made by GPT-4o on the <span id="A1.F78.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Correctness</span> attribute. The ’Chosen’ rationale contains an algebraic error but is incorrectly assigned a perfect score of 1.0, while the ’Rejected’ rationale, which only restates the prompt, is correctly scored as 0.0.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
